===============================================================================
THIRD-PARTY CODE
===============================================================================

This covers the source in this repository. Its dependencies are licensed by
their own authors under their own terms, and nothing here changes them. The two
that matter:

  @whiskeysockets/baileys   MIT
  whatsapp-rust-bridge      MIT

`shims/libsignal/` deliberately replaces the npm package `libsignal`, which is
GPL-3.0 and is not installed. Nothing in this repository is derived from it:
`src/curve.js` forwards to `whatsapp-rust-bridge`, `src/crypto.js` is written
from the published standards (AES-256-CBC, HMAC-SHA256, SHA-512, and HKDF as
RFC 5869 specifies it), and `src/protobufs.js` decodes one field from a wire
format that is a published specification. Correctness is pinned by known-answer
vectors rather than by shared code — see README.md.
